      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T20:50:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One side-effect of this change has been that we have now doubled the size of the history buffer whenever 4-byte port80 codes are used. Wouldn\u0027t it be sufficient to print the port80 code correctly for `print_in_int` mode, but in the deferred mode, just print it byte-by-byte? I suspect that close to 50% of our history buffer is now going to be just 0s for the platforms that select 4-byte port80 messages. Is the additional space usage really worth it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "14dd51f4fcfeb1bbbdbf0dd9f9365c4072db44ef",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c48093ad_2edd4d04",
        "filename": "common/port80.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T02:18:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These means, in the deferred mode, we should divide the 4 byte code to 4 1-byte and put them in the history array. However, with the current port_80_write function which passes only one parameter \"data\", we cannot know if data is 1-byte or 4-byte.\n(Note: per comment form Rob, AMD CEZANNE will send 4-byte and 1-byte code at different stage. This means we cannot assume that it is either 4-byte or 1-byte.)",
      "parentUuid": "868c8f77_3fdc3eb0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "14dd51f4fcfeb1bbbdbf0dd9f9365c4072db44ef",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "217a68ec_b0ea03bd",
        "filename": "common/port80.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T02:23:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, basically, I was wondering if it is okay to display the 4-byte code correctly only when `int_in_print` is true. In deferred mode, we could just dump the code as a 1-byte code i.e. 4 bytes one after the other. We can always massage it so that the MSB is pushed into history buffer before LSB so that it visually appears correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "c48093ad_2edd4d04",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "14dd51f4fcfeb1bbbdbf0dd9f9365c4072db44ef",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
